I think the ability to see monsters through walls is the most valuable
       thing. If i had to choose between HoT and GDSM, i think i would
       take HoT. Would you ?

     o an amulet of life saving

This wont be very usefull for a few times, but
     - I'm thinking at the Wizard and his touch of death ('cause with
       such a start, i *must* win :-)
     - I want to know *which* amulet is the good one.

     o 3 cursed scrolls of genocide

This was new for me. I wanted to see what i could do with nurses.
So, I went back up one level (ie level 2), went in the small room at
the east, closed and locked the doors (Oh yes, i also found a
lock-pick and a blindfold in the shop. And there was a stetoscope, but
i hadn't enough gold, and i dont wanted to kill the 'keeper
(priest=>neutral). And then, let's play with nurses.

  The 3 scrolls of genocides boosted my HP from 36 to 118 !!!
(A note here : having a HoT and a blindfold was of most use here,
since nurses, as i learnt, usualy teleport in the level after a few
good-time with you. And walking nacked in the dungeon to go and play
again with them is most pearilous if you don't know where they are and
where the others monsters are).



Part II : A few comments
-------      

While speaking of GDSM : a few days ago, i saw someone asking why he
couldn't obtain a GDSM by polymorphing a GD corpse (He could only get
a tin a GD meat). I thought that GDSM could only be obtain by wish,
and not by polymorphing. Am I right ?

I thought (cf WCST spolier manual) that Mjollnir was doing dammages
with +24 bonus. But using the stetoscope, i noticed that, during many
levels, i was only doing about 12 HP dammage. At the end of the game,
with exp-level 15, and +6 Mjollnir, I was able to do >= 40 Hp.  Can
somebody explain ?
This is the first time that i'm playing with Mjollnir; I used to play
a valkiry with Stromy, but I thought a Hammer would be better for a
Priest.


There is nothing particular to mention during my way down to the
castle, except :

  o I #dipped my long sword as soon as possible (ie level 5) in order
to gain Excalibur. I didn't used it (i wanted to test Mjollnir) except
agains Wraith and Vampires, in order to prevent level-drain.

  o I found another magic-lamp, and got :
     = 2 blessed scrolls of charging. (So, I still have one left for
         the wand of the castle).
     = a blessed bag of holding.

A note here : I know that there is a dirty trick with cursing the BoH,
but i don't know the details exactly; so i prefered to ask for a
blessed one. I tested it a little and learned that a blessed bag was
dividing the weight of thing by three (ie : a scroll weights 3000 $
out of the bag, and 1000 $ in the bag).

  o I meet 2 priests, and got my AC reduced by 6 by #chating with them

An other note : I discovered that you may have your AC reduced by
#chating with a priest of another alignement (a chaotic in this case),
even if you don't convert it's altar to your religion, and this
while staying in good relation ship with your god.
I #chat after that with a priest of my religion and my ac was reduced
too.



